<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Okeechobee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Okeechobee is the largest freshwater lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, in the south of the state, feeding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/everglades">Everglades</a> to its south. Its basin was home to the Belle Glade culture, whose people built earthworks and canals and paid tribute to the Calusa. The Battle of Lake Okeechobee in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-seminole-war">Second Seminole War</a> was fought on its shore in 1837, and after deadly hurricanes in 1926 and 1928 it was enclosed by the Herbert Hoover Dike.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-okeechobee.jpg" alt="Lake Okeechobee" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Florida_Lac_Okeechobee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
